  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water for Peace in Yemen: Strengthening the Role of Women in Water Conflict Resolution and Resource Management across the HDPN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will address the immediate risks of water scarcity and conflict whilst at the same time working on the establishment of adaptive pathways to manage and mitigate the risks of flooding and environmental degradation. IOM will contribute to improved capacity among target communities in Hadramawt to mitigate and manage water-related conflicts, with an emphasis on infrastructure rehabilitation and establishment of community-led conflict resolution mechanisms. IOM will also support long-term resilience of target communities by providing livelihood opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
